## ENUMS(ENUMERATORS) ## 
in Java is a special data type used to define a fixed, type-safe collection of constants
Under the hood, Java enums are full-featured classes that implicitly extend java.lang.Enum


To define a basic enum, use the enum keyword instead of class or interface
public enum Level {
    LOW, 
    MEDIUM, 
    HIGH
}

Level currentLevel = Level.MEDIUM;

// Enums work natively with switch statements
switch (currentLevel) {
    case LOW -> System.out.println("Low level");
    case MEDIUM -> System.out.println("Medium level");
    case HIGH -> System.out.println("High level");
}

Because every enum automatically extends java.lang.Enum, it inherits several built-in methods
values(): Returns an array containing all the constants in the enum.
valueOf(String name): Converts a matching string precisely into its corresponding enum constant
ordinal(): Returns the sequential index position of the constant, starting at 0.
name(): Returns the exact string name of the constant.

------------------------
java enums can contain fields, methods, and constructors. This lets you attach state and behavior directly to your constants

 public enum TrafficLight {
    RED("Stop"), 
    YELLOW("Caution"), 
    GREEN("Go");

    // Private field to hold state
    private final String action;

    // Constructors must be private. Java enforces this automatically.
    private TrafficLight(String action) {
        this.action = action;
    }

    // Public getter method
    public String getAction() {
        return this.action;
    }
}

// in main method 
String redAction = TrafficLight.RED.getAction(); // Returns "Stop"

